## Exp41 — Shared Discrete-Time Competing-Risk Survival Law — FULL PASS

Question: can one TRAIN-fitted law replace four horizon-specific models?

```text
BASE_SURV:
 ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k]
 REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k]

POSITION_SURV:
 ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k] + beta_ADV_geo*geo0
 REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k] + beta_REC_geo*geo0

SEMI_SURV:
 ADV vs STAY = alpha_ADV[k] + beta_ADV_geo*geo0 + beta_ADV_dwell*dwell0
 REC vs STAY = alpha_REC[k] + beta_REC_geo*geo0 + beta_REC_dwell*dwell0
```

`k=1..24` future M5 steps; Position/Dwell coefficients shared across all future steps; starting covariates frozen at state_time.

TRAIN person-period:

```text
67550 at-risk rows
STAY=63795 | ADVANCE=1559 | RECAPTURE=2196
```

Shared TRAIN coefficients:

```text
POSITION_SURV
beta_ADV_geo = +0.48459159
beta_REC_geo = -0.46233758

SEMI_SURV
beta_ADV_geo   = +0.56488735
beta_ADV_dwell = -0.49064436
beta_REC_geo   = -0.38927814
beta_REC_dwell = -0.34241833
```

Pooled scores:

```text
VALIDATION
BASE_SURV      Brier .551497773 | LL .935442929
POSITION_SURV  Brier .486803505 | LL .819316481
SEMI_SURV      Brier .457326565 | LL .773670357

TEST
BASE_SURV      Brier .541519940 | LL .921174237
POSITION_SURV  Brier .477243267 | LL .795857298
SEMI_SURV      Brier .434070949 | LL .734149938
```

Frozen inference:

```text
Gate A POSITION_SURV vs BASE_SURV
VAL  Brier +0.064694268 CI[+0.049262455,+0.083489471]
VAL  LL    +0.116126448 CI[+0.089068821,+0.148688916]
TEST Brier +0.064276674 CI[+0.044789535,+0.087118857]
TEST LL    +0.125316939 CI[+0.095287646,+0.161435467]
4/4 PASS

Gate B SEMI_SURV vs POSITION_SURV
VAL  Brier +0.029476939 CI[+0.009247834,+0.052242895]
VAL  LL    +0.045646123 CI[+0.016119684,+0.078881841]
TEST Brier +0.043172318 CI[+0.017482273,+0.068635147]
TEST LL    +0.061707360 CI[+0.023525791,+0.100625463]
4/4 PASS

SHARED_SURVIVAL_CORRIDOR_LAW = PASS
```

Cumulative coherence: `P(NO_EXIT)` non-increasing 100%; `CIF_ADV/CIF_REC` non-decreasing 100%; probability-sum error ~1e-15.

Interpretation: most multi-horizon information is representable by one coherent shared survival law. Historical exploratory only; not a trading-rule backtest.

